%N A401165 Largest possible gap between adjacent elements of cyclic planar difference sets over Z_(m^2+m+1), m = A000961(n).
%C A401165 These sets have m+1 elements, and m is called their order. They are also called perfect difference sets.
%C A401165 Perfect difference sets are subsets of an additive group with the property that every nonzero group element can be expressed as a difference of two difference set elements in exactly one way.
%C A401165 James Singer (1938) gave an algebraic construction for m a prime power. No other solutions are known. It is conjectured that all such sets are Singer type.
%C A401165 It is known that m must be a prime power if it is less than 2 million (Daniel M. Gordon, 1994).
%C A401165 Individual sets of same order can have different largest gaps. This series is the overall maximum.
%C A401165 The length of a Golomb ruler constructed from a perfect difference set is its modulus minus its largest gap, thus the best rulers obtainable from difference sets have length A333865(n)-a(n).
%C A401165 Terms a(n) for 8 < n <= 2000 have been calculated based on the Singer conjecture. The author acknowledges support by the state of Baden-Württemberg through bwHPC.
%H A401165 Martin Becker, <a href="/A401165/b401165.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..2000</a>
%H A401165 Daniel M. Gordon, <a href="https://doi.org/10.37236/1186">The Prime Power Conjecture Is True for n<2000000</a>, Elec. J. Combin. 1, R6, (1994).
%H A401165 James Singer, <a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/1990067?seq=1/">A Theorem in Finite Projective Geometry and Some Applications to Number Theory</a>, Trans. AMS, 43 (1938) 377-385, Table on p. 384.
%H A401165 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PerfectDifferenceSet.html">Perfect Difference Set</a>.
%e A401165 Perfect difference sets of order 4 = A000961(4) over Z_21 are {0, 1, 4, 14, 16} (mod 21) and {0, 1, 6, 8, 18} (mod 21) and their translates. Gaps between adjacent elements, including the wrap-around from the last element back to the first, are (1, 3, 10, 2, 5) and (1, 5, 2, 10, 3). Hence, a(4) = 10, the maximum of these gaps.
%Y A401165 Cf. A333852, A335866, A333865, A000961.
